  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><img src=\"assets\\st0020_b66a57ef10c6.png\" style=\"width: 300px; height: 164px;\" /><br />Clearly,&nbsp;<math><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math> is local maximum<br />If <math><mi>f</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>⇒</mo><msup><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>-</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></math><br /><math><mo>⇒</mo><msup><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>-</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>D</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mfenced><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0</mn></math><br /><math><mo>⇒</mo></math> No real solution<br />Also, <math><mi>f</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> is increasing&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>∀</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mi>∞</mi></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;and in <math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi></mi><mi>π</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>,</mo></math></p><p>but decreasing in <math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></math></p>"
